Contents of "Base1:" directory...

    - This directory contains all my Fido Message echoes, including these
      four, which I HIGHLY advise you to also carry:

        BAD_MSGS

            - Similar to the BADFILES directory in the UDBase0: directory,
              this area can be used to store duplicate messages, as well as
              overflow messages(in case a particular base is full). This is
              also the area where unknown messages will be copied(in the
              event CNet can't locate a needed message area).

            - There are two options dealing with "bad", located in the
              "Tosser..." section of CNet's Config. You should checkmark
              these two options if you wish to take full advantage of this
              base, while running your network(s).

        CNET
        CNET_BBS
        JAMMAIL

            - These three should be carried for OBVIOUS reasons. If you have
              not already done so, I highly suggest you AreaFix these from
              your Boss soon!

        BaseSizes

            - This file is created by the "BaseSizes" file, located in the
              "pfiles:fido/" directory. It simply talleys the file sizes for
              all fido message echoes carried on your bbs. I use it as the
              entry screen into my Fido Message Area.

